traceability.evidence:
Story file exists and matches the provided specification:
  - docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
  Content confirms the same acceptance criteria and requirements (REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE, REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION, REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION, REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC, REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES, REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE).,Rule implementation updated to support JSDoc coexistence and boundaries:
  - src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts
    - processCommentLine(...) now integrates generic JSDoc-tag boundary handling:
      """
      import {
        PendingAnnotation,
        normalizeCommentLine,
        isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine,
      } from "./helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal";
      ...
      // Implement JSDoc tag coexistence behavior: terminate @story/@req values when a new non-traceability JSDoc tag line (e.g., @param, @returns) is encountered.
      // @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
      if (isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized)) {
        finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
        return null;
      }
      ...
      if (pending) {
        const continuation = normalized.trim();
        if (!continuation) {
          return pending;
        }
        const updatedValue = pending.value
          ? `${pending.value} ${continuation}`
          : continuation;
        return {
          ...pending,
          value: updatedValue,
          hasValue: pending.hasValue || continuation.length > 0,
        };
      }
      """
    - This logic:
      - Terminates any pending @story/@req value when encountering a non-traceability JSDoc tag line (REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION, REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC).
      - Only continues multi-line values on lines that do not start with another JSDoc tag (AC: Continuation Lines).,JSDoc tag boundary detection helper implements generic @word detection and excludes traceability tags:
  - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts
    - normalizeCommentLine(rawLine: string):
      """
      const trimmed = rawLine.trim();
      if (!trimmed) return "";
      const filtered = trimmed.replace(/`[^`]*`/g, ...);
      const annotationMatch = filtered.match(/@story\b|@req\b|@supports\b/);
      if (!annotationMatch || annotationMatch.index === undefined) {
        const withoutLeadingStar = filtered.replace(/^\*\s?/, "");
        return withoutLeadingStar;
      }
      return filtered.slice(annotationMatch.index);
      """
      - For lines without @story/@req/@supports (e.g. `* @param ...`), returns the line starting from `@param`, preserving JSDoc tag structure while stripping leading `*`.
      - Preserves line boundaries and does not collapse across lines, fixing the original newline-concatenation issue (REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION, REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE).
    - isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string):
      """
      const trimmed = normalized.trimStart();
      if (!trimmed || !trimmed.startsWith("@")) {
        return false;
      }
      if (/^@(story|req|supports)\b/.test(trimmed)) {
        return false;
      }
      return true;
      """
      - Recognizes any line beginning with `@` as a JSDoc tag, except `@story`, `@req`, `@supports` (REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION, REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE).
      - Combined with processCommentLine, this ensures **any** other JSDoc tag (@param, @returns, @throws, etc.) terminates multi-line traceability values (AC: JSDoc Tag Detection, Proper Termination).,Tests explicitly tied to this story and its requirements exist and pass:
